# Line-ending policy.
#
# Bash hooks and Python scripts are executed on Linux hosts even when the
# checkout happens on Windows (e.g. a WSL `claude` installing this plugin
# from a /mnt/c working-tree marketplace). CRLF bash scripts fail to parse
# there with exit 2 — which, for the Stop hook, Claude Code interprets as
# "block the stop" and loops headless sessions. Force LF so every checkout
# is safe to reuse across platforms.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# PowerShell parity hooks are Windows-native; platform-default endings.
*.ps1 text
